<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saskatchewan</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Saskatchewan is a prairie province of western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/canada">Canada</a>, between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alberta">Alberta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manitoba">Manitoba</a>, with Regina as its capital. Formerly part of Rupert's Land and the North-West Territories, it was the scene of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-west-rebellion">North-West Rebellion</a> of 1885 and became a province in 1905. It is a leading producer of wheat, potash and uranium.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saskatchewan.jpg" alt="Saskatchewan" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Kooma · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Saskatchewan.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>Alberta and <b>Saskatchewan</b> became provinces in 1905, and Newfoundland joined after referendums in 1949.</blockquote><a href="/empire/canada">Canada · Governance &amp; Law</a></li><li><blockquote>In the Cree uprising of the North-West Rebellion, Cree men led by Wandering Spirit attacked the small settlement of Frog Lake, in the District of <b>Saskatchewan</b> of the North-West Territories, and killed nine officials, clergy and settlers.</blockquote><a href="/today-in-history/april-2">2 April in history</a></li><li><blockquote>Guns from the fur trade gave them an early advantage, and they controlled access to trading posts along the <b>Saskatchewan</b> and Red rivers.</blockquote><a href="/state/iron-confederacy">Iron Confederacy</a></li><li><blockquote>The grant covered much of what is now northern Quebec and Ontario, Manitoba, <b>Saskatchewan</b>, Alberta and parts of the northern United States, though the company knew little of the interior.</blockquote><a href="/state/ruperts-land">Rupert's Land</a></li></ul></section>
